  "description": "The 158 Poor Law Unions of Ireland just before partition, drawn on the 1 Apr 1921 DED edition (Connacht 1919, Leinster 1919, Munster 1907, Ulster 1921 nine-county). No census was taken in 1921, so each 1921 DED takes the union of the 1911 DEDs it overlies (every one lies 98% or more in one union, Portrush Urban apart). The acreage and population are the 1911 census figures. The Dáil Éireann county schemes of 1921-22, which closed or merged many southern unions, came later. In the six counties the cross-border unions were reorganised on 1 Apr 1921; see Poor Law Unions (Northern Ireland).",
